{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Subring.Basic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.mul'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.mul'","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L419-L435","doc":"`IsClose` is multiplicative on the **finite** subset:\nif `x` and `y'` are finite, `x ~ x'` and `y ~ y'` then\n`x * y ~ x' * y'`.\n\nThe finiteness hypotheses are necessary: an infinite × infinitesimal\ncan have any standard part, breaking the implication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.sub'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.sub'","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L410-L417","doc":"`IsClose` is preserved by subtraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.add'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.add'","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L400-L408","doc":"`IsClose` is additive: if `x ~ x'` and `y ~ y'` then\n`x + y ~ x' + y'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.neg'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.neg'","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L392-L398","doc":"`IsClose` is preserved by negation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.isClose_iff_standardPart_eq_of_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.isClose_iff_standardPart_eq_of_finite","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L362-L384","doc":"`IsClose x y ↔ standardPart x = standardPart y` when `x, y` are\nboth finite (forward + reverse direction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_eq_of_isClose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_eq_of_isClose","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L348-L360","doc":"**Standard-part is constant on `IsClose`-equivalence classes**\n(for finite arguments). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.setoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.setoid","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L343-L346","doc":"`IsClose` as an equivalence relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose.trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose.trans","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L335-L341","doc":"`IsClose` is transitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose.symm","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L328-L333","doc":"`IsClose` is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose.refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose.refl","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L322-L326","doc":"`IsClose` is reflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.IsClose","kind":"def","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L319-L320","doc":"Two surreals are **close** if their difference is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPartRingHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPartRingHom","kind":"def","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L295-L306","doc":"Robinson's **standard-part map** as a `RingHom` from the\nfinite-surreal subring of `K` to `ℝ`.  Bundles\n`standardPart_zero`, `standardPart_one`, `standardPart_add`, and\n`standardPart_mul` into a single `RingHom` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.mem_finiteSubring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.mem_finiteSubring","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L289-L293","doc":"Membership in `finiteSubring` is exactly `IsFinite`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.finiteSubring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.finiteSubring","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L278-L287","doc":"The **finite-surreal subring** of `K`.  Closure follows from\n`zero_isFinite`, `one_isFinite`, `IsFinite.add`, `IsFinite.neg`,\n`IsFinite.mul` (proved in `Basic.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_le_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_le_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L191-L269","doc":"Standard-part preserves order (weakly) on the finite subring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_mul","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L135-L189","doc":"Standard-part is multiplicative on the finite subring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_add","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L109-L133","doc":"Standard-part is additive on the finite subring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_of_infinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_of_infinitesimal","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L98-L107","doc":"An infinitesimal has standard part zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L93-L96","doc":"The standard part of one is one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L88-L91","doc":"The standard part of zero is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L73-L86","doc":"The standard part of a real is itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ofReal_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ofReal_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L55-L71","doc":"`ofReal r` is finite for any real `r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_spec","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L46-L53","doc":"Defining property: for finite `x`, `x - ofReal (st x)` is\ninfinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.termSt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.termSt","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L43-L44","doc":"Notation: `st x = standardPart x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/StandardPart.lean#L35-L41","doc":"Robinson's **standard-part map**: sends each finite surreal to the\nunique real of which it is an infinitesimal perturbation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:standard-part-functor","label":"def:standard-part-functor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/standard-part-functor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}